title VerificationEvidence status (verification_evidence.status)
[*] --> PENDING : submitLecturerVerification(),\nrequestVerification(),\nstudent-affiliation submit
[*] --> VERIFIED : institutional email domain match\n(affiliation.service)
PENDING --> VERIFIED : decideVerification()\napprove
PENDING --> NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION : decideVerification()\nmore_info
PENDING --> REJECTED : decideVerification()\nreject
PENDING --> INVALIDATED : profile position, institution\nor identity changed
NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION --> INVALIDATED : position or affiliation\ntarget changed
NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION --> NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION : superseded (supersededAt set)\nwhen user resubmits
VERIFIED --> VERIFIED : position change sets\ninvalidatedAt only
REJECTED --> [*]
INVALIDATED --> [*]
state UNVERIFIED #F5F5F5
state NOT_SUBMITTED #F5F5F5
state EXPIRED #F5F5F5
note right of PENDING
  Rows are created directly as PENDING (or VERIFIED by email
  domain match). Resubmission after NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION
  creates a NEW row (revision+1, previousRequestId) in PENDING.
end note
note bottom of NOT_SUBMITTED
  <b>Dead values</b>: UNVERIFIED, NOT_SUBMITTED and EXPIRED are
  allowed by the DB CHECK constraint but no code writes them
  on this table. Retention cleanup removes files only; it
  does not set EXPIRED.
end note
@enduml
